## Description

I am trying to validate over 200 dataframes using pointblank, and wish to print a gt-based report for each dataframe inside a single rmarkdown document.

I have a list of interrogated agents, where each element in that list corresponds to a single interrogated agent.

I would like to print all elements of the list with a single command, however, the only way I can get the gt-table to render correctly is if I access each element of the list using square brackets -- which means have to copy and paste and iterate through each element manually.

When I try printing the tables by executing the name of the list in the console, the table won't render at all without setting chunk opts to `results = 'asis'`. When the chunk options for results are set to `asis`, the table renders, but with the same behaviour described in the next example:

When I use `purrr::map()` or `lapply()` with `pointblank::get_agent_report()` (in conjunction with setting the chunk opts to `results = 'asis'`), the table renders incompletely for validation steps that have a value supplied to the `label` argument.

## Reproducible example

Since the code returns output as expected when executed in console, but does not render as expected within rmarkdown documents, I have provided an Rmarkdown document in a gist. This file contains the code chunks, and relevant chunk options specified to reproduce the behaviour I have described above: https://gist.github.com/egouldo/605a1147e31d95846c08c331046301f1

For a quick glance at the code contained in the rmarkdown doc:

```r
data("small_table")

df <- tibble(id = c(1,2), data = list(small_table))

validate_small_table <- function(data){
  al <- action_levels(warn_at = 0.1, stop_at = 0.2)
  
  agent <- 
  create_agent(
    tbl = small_table,
    tbl_name = "small_table",
    label = "VALID-I Example No. 2",
    actions = al
  ) %>%
  col_is_posix(vars(date_time),label = "check that date_time col is posix") %>%
  col_vals_in_set(vars(f), set = c("low", "mid")) %>%
  col_vals_lt(vars(a), value = 7) %>%
  col_vals_regex(vars(b), regex = "^[0-9]-[a-w]{3}-[2-9]{3}$") %>%
  col_vals_between(vars(d), left = 0, right = 4000) %>%
  interrogate()
  
  return(agent)
}


validate_small_table(small_table)

df <- tibble(id = c(1,2), data = list(small_table)) %>% 
  mutate(result = map(.x = data, .f = ~ validate_small_table(.x)))

df$result # will not render without setting 'results = 'asis'' in chunk opts

df$result[[1]] # renders without setting 'results = 'asis'' in chunk opts

df$result %>%  map(get_agent_report) # does not render without specifying results opt
```

```{r results='asis'}
df$result %>%  map(get_agent_report) # renders, but not completely
```

# Expected and Actual Output

**Expected output for each element in the reproducible example is:**

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8400682/110291906-915d3880-8040-11eb-9d1f-bc716345f889.png)

**Actual output where partial render occurs  (when chunk opts set correctly):**

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8400682/110292041-c073aa00-8040-11eb-96d1-bbfa15e9d025.png)

**Output where table render does not occur (when chunk opts not set + when attempting to render tables from a list):**

```r
df$result %>%  map(get_agent_report) # does not render without specifying results opt
```

